# ============================================================================
# DELAYED SIGNAL - A One-Step Time Delay
# ============================================================================
# Description: The simplest temporal operation. The output at time t is the input
# from the PREVIOUS time step (t-1) - a one-step delay line. It demonstrates how a
# rule can look back in time with the [t-1] index.

# === STREAMS ===
i1 : sbf := in file("io/signal.in")     # input signal, one bit per line
o1 : sbf := out file("io/delayed.out")  # the same signal, delayed by one step

# === THE RULE ===
# output at time t = input at time t-1
r o1[t] = i1[t-1]

# === HOW IT BEHAVES ===
# At step 0 there is no previous input yet (i1[-1]), so the output starts at 0.
# From step 1 on, each output simply repeats the input of the step before.
#
# Example: io/signal.in = 1,0,1,0
#   step  : 0 1 2 3
#   input : 1 0 1 0
#   output: 0 1 0 1     (input shifted right by one; step 0 = 0)
